      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by noting that \\(\\alpha\\) is inversely proportional to \\(\\beta\\). This relationship can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[\n\\alpha \\beta = k\n\\]\nwhere \\(k\\) is a constant. We are given that \\(\\alpha = 4\\) when \\(\\beta = 9\\). We can use this information to find the value of \\(k\\).\n\nSubstituting \\(\\alpha = 4\\) and \\(\\beta = 9\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 9 = k \\implies k = 36\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the constant \\(k\\), we can use it to find \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\). Using the equation \\(\\alpha \\beta = k\\), we substitute \\(\\beta = -72\\) and \\(k = 36\\):\n\\[\n\\alpha \\cdot (-72) = 36\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\alpha\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{36}{-72} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]",
